.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-POLICY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-policy - Manage permission to activate a private port on demand


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel policy [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage permission to open a private port on a machine when someone asks for it, without
making a tunnel first. A policy authorizes one exact machine port for private or team access. It
never publishes a public URL and never opens other ports of the machine. Revoking a policy
blocks later activations. If the application behind an approved port is replaced, the new one
inherits access; Paperboat does not start the application.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for policy


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel policy allow homelab 3000
  pb tunnel policy list
  pb tunnel policy revoke pol_abc
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-policy-allow(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-policy-get(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-policy-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-tunnel-policy-revoke(1)\fP
